# RULE: Feature Registry

This is a mandatory Cursor rule.

Every product change must map to `docs/softphone/Feature-Registry.md`.

## Required Before Implementation

Before creating or changing code, identify:

- Feature ID
- feature name
- bounded context
- priority
- status
- acceptance criteria
- test coverage

If the feature does not exist, update the registry first.

## No Orphan Functionality

Never add:

- new UI behavior
- new Use Case
- new Domain Event
- new adapter
- new repository
- new IPC channel
- new host-page event
- new store projection

without a Feature Registry entry.

## Registry Update Required

Update the registry when:

- a feature is added
- a feature is removed
- a feature changes behavior
- acceptance criteria change
- test strategy changes
- status changes
- ownership changes

## Feature Scope

Each feature must belong to one primary bounded context:

- Telephony
- Operator
- Media
- Headset
- Settings
- Integration

If a feature spans multiple contexts, document the primary context and integration points.

## Acceptance Criteria

Acceptance criteria must describe observable behavior.

Good:

- `Incoming call produces IncomingCallReceived and appears in ringing projection.`
- `SIP-only mode starts without OCP plugin.`

Bad:

- `Implement incoming call.`
- `Refactor provider.`

## Test Coverage

Each feature must define:

- unit coverage
- integration coverage
- E2E coverage or explicit deferral reason

If a feature is critical, at least unit and integration coverage are required.

## Refactoring

Refactoring must preserve all affected Feature Registry entries.

Before refactoring:

- list affected features
- list affected events
- list affected external contracts

After refactoring:

- verify acceptance criteria still hold
- update registry if behavior changed

## Completion Check

Do not finish a task until:

- registry entry exists
- feature status is correct
- acceptance criteria are current
- tests match the registry
